WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:08.800
What stands out to you, as you look back on your career, as your single best accomplishment?

2
00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:15.960
There’s no doubt about that: it was the Tulane ball game of ’49.

3
00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:23.320
As I say, Tulane had . . . Even if we beat them, they had still won the conference championship.

4
00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:26.680
They were a twenty-one-point favorite.

5
00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:30.840
And if I could have stayed home and sent the football team down there to play that game,

6
00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:35.780
I think I would have because that’s how bad everybody, including myself, thought we might get beat.

7
00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:38.100
Of course, we were hoping for better than that.

8
00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:41.740
But we went down there and beat them twenty-one to nothing.

9
00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:47.600
And they were a twenty-one-point favorite, too, to beat us.

10
00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:54.840
I personally think that is the best football game that any LSU team has ever played.

11
00:00:54.840 --> 00:01:00.860
I doubt if anybody has ever beaten the point spread by forty-two points.

12
00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:05.660
It was . . . Just everything went right for us.

13
00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:08.280
Everybody on our team had a great game.

14
00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:11.080
They [Tulane] didn’t have anybody that had a particularly great one.

15
00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:16.040
Just really as near a perfect football game as you can find.

16
00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:18.580
Were there some outstanding plays?

17
00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:18.920
Yes.

18
00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:25.780
Kenny Konz returned a punt for about seventy yards.

19
00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:28.490
And Lee Hedges ran, I guess, about sixty-five.

20
00:01:28.490 --> 00:01:34.780
I mean, offhand, I don’t recall how we scored the other touchdown but then we had two long runs.

21
00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:39.640
I imagine if you take the film today and go through the entire film,

22
00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:47.060
I think that every tackle that was made . . . that we made on a Tulane player,

23
00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:56.000
I bet you that on every tackle there would be at least three people close enough that they could have made the tackle if the men made it.

24
00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:00.480
As I say, it’s just one of those days that everything you did was right.

25
00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:03.600
How do you think you get a team up to that level?

26
00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:05.760
You don’t very often.

27
00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:09.240
I never did get one up to that level except that one time.

28
00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:11.820
And I don’t think many people have ever gotten one up to that level.

29
00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:17.060
They were . . . as I say they just . . . You know when you’re a twenty-one-point underdog,

30
00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:25.680
and you win by twenty-one and the other team doesn’t even . . . I don’t know if they ever crossed our forty-yard line.

31
00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:28.300
And they were . . . They were a fine football team!

32
00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:30.700
I mean, we weren’t even supposed to be on the field with them.

33
00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:32.340
I mean, there weren’t any big breaks.

34
00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:37.420
There just . . . We just out-played them that much from start to finish.

35
00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:38.900
Of course, we did get two long runs.

36
00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:43.900
But we didn’t have a turnover, didn’t have any of that to help us any.
